Code adapted from eMule
-----------------------

eMule, Copyright (C) 2002-2010 Merkur (devteam at emule-project.net, http://www.emule-project.net);
its Kademlia code: Copyright (C) 2003 Barry Dunne, (C) 2002 Petar Maymounkov, (C) 2004-2010
Merkur. Licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 or (at your option) any later
version. Reference version: eMule 0.50a (source mirror
https://github.com/irwir/eMule, commit 88a8c8f). OctoMX uses it under GPL-3.0-or-later as
that licence permits.

Parts of these files are adapted (re-written in C++17/Qt, following eMule's structure and
control flow; no file was copied verbatim) from the eMule sources named in parentheses:

  src/net/ed2k/kad/kad_routing.cpp  Kad routing table: contact type ageing, zone add/split/
                                    consolidate, small/big timers (kademlia/routing/Contact.cpp,
                                    RoutingZone.cpp, RoutingBin.cpp)
  src/net/ed2k/kad/kad_search.cpp   Kad lookup state machine and keyword splitting
                                    (kademlia/kademlia/Search.cpp, SearchManager.cpp)
  src/net/ed2k/kad/kad_node.cpp     Kad packet flood tracking and the HELLO handler sequencing
                                    (kademlia/net/PacketTracking.cpp, KademliaUDPListener.cpp)
  src/net/ed2k/kad/kad_wire.cpp     Kad UDP de-obfuscation key-try order
                                    (EncryptedDatagramSocket.cpp)
  src/net/ed2k/ed2k_crypto.cpp      obfuscated TCP stream negotiation and the random protocol
                                    marker (EncryptedStreamSocket.cpp)
  src/net/ed2k/ed2k_upload.cpp      UDP file re-ask handling (ClientUDPSocket.cpp)
  src/net/ed2k/ed2k_peer.cpp        client software/version detection (BaseClient.cpp)

In addition, several files use eMule's protocol identifiers (opcode/tag names and values, the
96-byte DH prime of the stream obfuscation, timing constants such as re-ask intervals and Kad
parameters) because interoperating with eMule-compatible clients requires them; and
src/hash/aich.cpp implements eMule's AICH hash-tree layout. Protocol facts like these are not
copied code, but they are credited here as well.


Other credits
-------------

* QRP keyword hash: from the public "Query Routing for the Gnutella Network" specification
  (LimeWire, C. Rohrs). The Gnutella module is an independent implementation; some behaviour
  parameters follow gtk-gnutella (GPL-2.0-or-later, https://gtk-gnutella.sourceforge.io),
  e.g. the THEX serving-depth thresholds and the 30-minute search re-query interval, and its
  default UDP host caches are a subset of gtk-gnutella's list.
* The eD2k seed server list comes from the eMule Security server.met (emule-security.org).
* Tiger: the key schedule follows the public-domain reference by R. Anderson and E. Biham.
* The user-interface font "OctoMX Tahoma" is derived from Wine's Tahoma (LGPL-2.1-or-later);
  see src/ui/res/fonts/ and third_party/fonts/.

Third-party libraries (Qt, libtorrent-rasterbar, OpenSSL, Boost, zlib, librats, ...) keep their
own licences. They are not part of this source tree (the build scripts download them), and the
binary packages list them in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt with their licence texts.
